{{!--
  GH-67 (S3): the dialog is wired up by src/js/12-search.ts — opening it from
  header-content.hbs's trigger, loading the site's search index (GH-65,
  fetched from `{{uiRootPath}}/search/` + `data-search-index` below), and
  populating/hiding the states below as the reader types. GH-66 (S2) shipped
  this shell as static markup only; that's no longer true.

  Guarded by `page.componentVersion.searchIndex` (same attribute
  header-content.hbs's trigger checks) — a component version with no search
  index gets no dialog to open, rather than one whose input and close button
  stay disabled forever.

  Included once from header.hbs, so it exists on every page — a dialog is a
  page-level overlay, not something that belongs to the header's own DOM
  subtree.

  `<dialog>` over a hand-rolled overlay + focus trap: `showModal()` gives the
  top layer, the platform focus trap, Esc-to-close and an implicit ::backdrop
  for free — the same things src/js/05-nav-modules.ts has to hand-roll for
  the side menu's drawer, because that one isn't a <dialog>. The DS's own
  `.ids-modal` CSS assumes its own React portal rather than a <dialog>;
  search-dialog.css resets the UA <dialog> box model to stand in for that
  portal's own fixed, full-viewport wrapper.

  The nesting below mirrors the DS's own `Overlay`/`Modal` composition
  exactly (`@inditex/sewingiopdsweb-react-components/overlay/overlay.js` +
  `modal/modal.js`) rather than approximating it: `Overlay` always renders
  `.ids-overlay__content` (the backdrop) and its `children` (here, the
  `.ids-modal` wrapper) as SIBLINGS, both inside `.ids-overlay`. That
  ordering is load-bearing — `.ids-overlay__content+*` (ids-components.css)
  is what gives the modal wrapper `position: relative`, which is what makes
  it paint *above* the backdrop. `.ids-overlay` itself is `position: fixed`
  with no z-index; a positioned descendant with `z-index: auto` always
  paints after a NON-positioned in-flow one in the same stacking context,
  regardless of DOM order — so a `.ids-modal__container` living outside
  `.ids-overlay` (an earlier version of this file did exactly that) is
  invisibly stuck BEHIND the backdrop: `document.elementFromPoint()` at any
  point inside it resolves to `.ids-overlay__content`, not the panel, so
  every click — chips included — silently lands on the backdrop instead.
  Get the nesting right and no explicit z-index is needed at all, same as
  upstream.

  Content area (`.ids-modal__content--scrollable`) ships empty: which of
  loading / results / empty-state it should hold is filled in by
  12-search.ts as the reader types, never pre-rendered here. All states are
  reviewed together, with fixture content, from the dedicated preview page
  (preview-src/layouts/search-dialog.hbs).

  GH-68 (S4): `.ids-modal--fullscreen` is added/removed by 12-search.ts
  (matchMedia against the project's own `m` boundary, the same pattern
  01-nav.ts uses for its own breakpoint-dependent behaviour), not authored
  here statically alongside `.ids-modal--small`. The two classes carry the
  same specificity in ids-components.css and `--fullscreen`'s rule comes
  later in that file, so it would win unconditionally at every breakpoint —
  including m/l — if both were simply present together; only one of the two
  is ever on the element at a time (on `.search-dialog__panel`, below — see
  its own comment). The floating button below is the xs-only trigger that
  opens this same dialog, alongside (not instead of) header-content.hbs's
  own trigger, which hides itself at xs — 12-search.ts wires up whichever of
  the two exists. Same `page.componentVersion.searchIndex` guard: a
  component version with no index gets neither trigger.

  GH-69 (S5): two additions, both build-time decisions like everything above.

  1. Module filter chips — rendered only under the exact condition
     nav-switcher.hbs uses for the same purpose (`page.navigation.[1]` +
     `.module`: more than one root nav tree, annotated by
     @inditextech/docouture-antora-extensions). A tree with no `startUrl` is a
     `switcher: false` landing nav, not a module, and is skipped here too —
     the same rule nav-switcher.hbs documents. A single-module site
     (starter, the CLI template) fails the condition and gets no row at all,
     no dead markup, no runtime branch. `data-category` on each chip is the
     exact string 12-search.ts compares against `hit.category` — both are
     the nav tree's own `title`, sourced the same way
     antora-extensions/lib/search-index.js derives a record's `category`.

  2. The combobox/listbox pairing the ARIA 1.2 combobox pattern needs:
     `role="combobox"` + `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`/`aria-autocomplete`
     on the input, `role="listbox"` + an id on the results container so rows
     12-search.ts renders can be referenced from `aria-activedescendant` on
     the input — the active row is reported there, not by moving DOM focus
     off the field, so typing and arrowing both keep working. The count
     region is `aria-live="polite"` and visually hidden, updated alongside
     the results themselves.
--}}
{{#if page.componentVersion.searchIndex}}
<dialog id="search-dialog" class="search-dialog" aria-label="Search" data-search-index="{{page.componentVersion.searchIndex}}">
  <div class="ids-overlay ids-overlay--visible search-dialog__overlay">
    <div class="ids-overlay__content"></div>
    {{!--
      `.ids-modal`/`.ids-modal--small` live here, on the sibling of
      `.ids-overlay__content` — not fused onto `<dialog>` itself, which is
      what earlier broke the stacking order (see this file's own header).
      `.ids-modal--fullscreen` is toggled on THIS element by 12-search.ts
      (GH-68), not on `<dialog>`.
    --}}
    <div class="ids-modal ids-modal--small search-dialog__panel">
      <div class="ids-modal__container search-dialog__container">
        <div class="ids-search-field-minimal ids-search-field-minimal--full-width search-dialog__field">
          <span class="ids-search-field-minimal__icon-start" aria-hidden="true">{{icon "actions" "search-outlined"}}</span>
          <div class="ids-search-field-minimal__input-wrapper">
            <div class="ids-search-field-minimal__input-container">
              <input type="search" class="ids-search-field-minimal__input" placeholder="Search the docs" aria-label="Search the docs"
                role="combobox" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-autocomplete="list"
                aria-controls="search-dialog-listbox" disabled>
            </div>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="ids-button ids-button--ghost ids-button--icon-only search-dialog__close" aria-label="Close search" disabled>
            <span class="ids-button__content">
              <span class="ids-button__icon ids-button__icon-icon">{{icon "actions" "close-large-outlined"}}</span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </div>
    {{#if (and page.navigation.[1] page.navigation.[0].module)}}
        <div class="search-dialog__chips" role="group" aria-label="Filter results by module">
          <button type="button" class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid ids-tag--selected search-dialog__chip" data-category="" aria-pressed="true">
            <span class="ids-tag__label">All</span>
          </button>
          {{#each page.navigation}}
          {{#if ./startUrl}}
          <button type="button" class="ids-tag ids-tag--solid search-dialog__chip" data-category="{{detag ./title}}" aria-pressed="false">
            <span class="ids-tag__label">{{{./title}}}</span>
          </button>
          {{/if}}
          {{/each}}
        </div>
    {{/if}}
        <div id="search-dialog-listbox" class="ids-modal__content ids-modal__content--scrollable search-dialog__results" role="listbox" aria-label="Search results"></div>
        <div class="search-dialog__status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div class="ids-modal__footer ids-modal__footer--horizontal search-dialog__footer">
          <span class="ids-modal__footer-left ids-text ids-text--detail-m search-dialog__hints">
            <kbd>&uarr;&darr;</kbd> navigate &middot; <kbd>&crarr;</kbd> select &middot; <kbd>esc</kbd> close
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
<div class="ids-floating-button-wrapper ids-floating-button-wrapper--viewport ids-floating-button-wrapper--end search-fab">
  <button type="button" class="ids-button ids-button--ghost ids-button--icon-only ids-floating-button search-fab__trigger" aria-label="Search" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="search-dialog">
    <span class="ids-button__content">
      <span class="ids-button__icon ids-button__icon-icon">{{icon "actions" "search-outlined"}}</span>
    </span>
  </button>
</div>
{{/if}}
